1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:03,700
[The Chemistry]

2
00:00:03,800 --> 00:00:06,570
Hello, I'm Bever, and I play "Jaab."

3
00:00:06,670 --> 00:00:08,860
Hi, I'm Tonliew, Methaphat Chimkul.

4
00:00:08,890 --> 00:00:11,900
I play "Jane," Jannarong Jullaphak.

5
00:00:11,920 --> 00:00:14,180
I'm Prince, and I play "Pun."

6
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:16,170
I'm Doasao. I play "Ai."

7
00:00:16,370 --> 00:00:18,790
Hello. I'm Jeng, Chotipat Suthadsanasoung.

8
00:00:18,810 --> 00:00:20,350
I play "Khanoon."

9
00:00:20,370 --> 00:00:22,630
I'm Jara, and I play "Chomphoo."

10
00:00:22,660 --> 00:00:25,630
[Tell us the synopsis of this series]

11
00:00:25,780 --> 00:00:29,090
Jaab is a director at 'J. Production.'

12
00:00:29,110 --> 00:00:30,690
One day...

13
00:00:30,710 --> 00:00:33,170
a new producer named Jane joins the team.

14
00:00:33,190 --> 00:00:35,880
And something sparks in Jaab
the moment he sees him.

15
00:00:35,900 --> 00:00:38,290
It's a kind of chemistry
he's never felt before.

16
00:00:38,310 --> 00:00:41,420
Jaab likes Jane because he's adorable.

17
00:00:41,460 --> 00:00:44,810
He seems delicate and tiny,

18
00:00:44,830 --> 00:00:47,380
with a soft, pure look.

19
00:00:47,410 --> 00:00:50,530
Then one day, Jaab finds out that

20
00:00:50,550 --> 00:00:51,920
Jane only sees him as a friend,

21
00:00:51,940 --> 00:00:53,180
and he's already talking to someone.

22
00:00:53,200 --> 00:00:53,950
Someone named "M."
[Goodnight, Jane]

23
00:00:53,970 --> 00:00:56,980
Jane hasn't decided who to choose yet.

24
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:00,570
Jaab is a friend who always makes him happy
whenever they're together.

25
00:01:00,790 --> 00:01:02,150
As for Mon,
[You're not okay with me talking to Mon?]

26
00:01:02,170 --> 00:01:04,380
the guy Jane's been talking to...

27
00:01:04,400 --> 00:01:06,730
Jane feels good about him
and thinks he can take care of him.

28
00:01:06,900 --> 00:01:08,810
After the heartbreak,

29
00:01:08,830 --> 00:01:10,200
he doesn't know what to do.

30
00:01:10,220 --> 00:01:12,410
If he slides in, he'll just end up
being the third wheel.

31
00:01:12,430 --> 00:01:14,200
So he decides to give up.

32
00:01:14,220 --> 00:01:18,520
There will be all kinds of challenges
for Jane and Jaab to overcome together.

33
00:01:18,540 --> 00:01:21,830
It's the story of these two characters
at this production house.

34
00:01:21,950 --> 00:01:24,310
It's the kind of love where
they have to hold back their feelings.

35
00:01:24,330 --> 00:01:25,540
It's a love story about...

36
00:01:25,550 --> 00:01:26,240
working adults.

37
00:01:26,300 --> 00:01:28,300
Stay tuned to find out how the story unfolds.

38
00:01:28,320 --> 00:01:31,280
[What's your character like?]

39
00:01:31,300 --> 00:01:33,730
Jaab is someone with a wild side.

40
00:01:33,790 --> 00:01:35,710
He's full of energy and fun to be around.

41
00:01:35,730 --> 00:01:38,310
He likes to tease people
and joke around with them.

42
00:01:38,330 --> 00:01:41,050
At first, I was a bit surprised because
Jaab teases Jane a lot, but...

43
00:01:41,070 --> 00:01:43,510
he doesn't seem harmful to me.

44
00:01:43,530 --> 00:01:44,490
He teases Jane in a cute way.

45
00:01:44,510 --> 00:01:46,390
When it comes to work, he's alright.

46
00:01:46,410 --> 00:01:47,480
He's good at what he does.

47
00:01:47,500 --> 00:01:49,390
He's got a great imagination.

48
00:01:49,410 --> 00:01:51,650
But when it's everyday life,

49
00:01:51,670 --> 00:01:52,870
he sometimes makes me think,

50
00:01:52,950 --> 00:01:56,010
"Wait, are there really people
like this in the world?"

51
00:01:56,030 --> 00:01:57,750
He's just so... clueless.

52
00:01:57,780 --> 00:01:59,710
He's fairly rude and speaks impulsively.

53
00:01:59,730 --> 00:02:02,170
He doesn't think before he speaks.

54
00:02:02,190 --> 00:02:03,950
He sees something
and says it out loud immediately.

55
00:02:03,970 --> 00:02:06,320
He's rarely careful with what he says.

56
00:02:06,340 --> 00:02:08,700
Jane is a very lonely person.

57
00:02:08,800 --> 00:02:10,010
He barely has any friends.

58
00:02:10,040 --> 00:02:13,680
His only friends are the trees and the sky.

59
00:02:13,700 --> 00:02:15,700
Though he does have one close friend

60
00:02:15,720 --> 00:02:18,530
from university named "Min."

61
00:02:18,550 --> 00:02:20,310
He was homeschooled

62
00:02:20,330 --> 00:02:22,850
because he was bullied
at a regular school as a child.

63
00:02:22,870 --> 00:02:25,030
So his parents had tutors
teach him at home

64
00:02:25,050 --> 00:02:26,980
so he wouldn't have to
deal with the bullying,

65
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:28,660
since he comes from a wealthy family.

66
00:02:28,680 --> 00:02:32,040
He's wealthy and well-educated.

67
00:02:32,070 --> 00:02:33,620
At first, Jaab didn't know...

68
00:02:33,630 --> 00:02:36,010
that Jane's house was on these huge hills.

69
00:02:36,030 --> 00:02:37,790
Until he went there and realized...

70
00:02:37,820 --> 00:02:40,490
that Jane owned several of the hills there.

71
00:02:40,510 --> 00:02:41,670
Jaab was shocked and went...

72
00:02:41,690 --> 00:02:44,030
"Whoa, is Jane a tycoon or what?"

73
00:02:44,050 --> 00:02:45,990
Then Jaab understood
why Jane was the way he was.

74
00:02:46,010 --> 00:02:47,690
He's actually a rich kid.

75
00:02:47,710 --> 00:02:49,670
Like, seriously rich.

76
00:02:49,690 --> 00:02:53,300
He's also the type who needs
to have everything organized in his head.

77
00:02:53,330 --> 00:02:54,590
One, two, three, four.

78
00:02:54,610 --> 00:02:56,310
He's the complete opposite of Jaab.

79
00:02:56,330 --> 00:02:59,200
Pun is Jaab's junior.

80
00:02:59,220 --> 00:03:01,320
He's kind of the kid
at the production house,

81
00:03:01,330 --> 00:03:02,550
always going...

82
00:03:02,560 --> 00:03:03,950
"Yes, yes." Something like that.

83
00:03:03,970 --> 00:03:06,820
But he's more mature than Jaab
when it comes to love.

84
00:03:06,840 --> 00:03:08,700
So Jaab often goes to him for love advice.

85
00:03:08,900 --> 00:03:12,130
Ai is a newcomer, just starting
his internship at the production house.

86
00:03:12,150 --> 00:03:13,600
He's interning as a producer.

87
00:03:13,620 --> 00:03:15,800
He's a cheerful,

88
00:03:15,820 --> 00:03:16,520
fresh,

89
00:03:16,530 --> 00:03:18,650
and passionate new face

90
00:03:18,670 --> 00:03:21,030
who really wants to
get along with his seniors.

91
00:03:21,050 --> 00:03:22,230
This character is just like me.

92
00:03:22,250 --> 00:03:25,030
He's got tons of energy,
almost too much.

93
00:03:25,050 --> 00:03:29,370
I have to act opposite Jaab
and bring out his chemistry.

94
00:03:29,430 --> 00:03:31,680
Let me just say that Jaab...

95
00:03:31,700 --> 00:03:32,570
is stupid!

96
00:03:32,590 --> 00:03:33,910
He's got no brain!

97
00:03:33,940 --> 00:03:35,360
He's an idiot!

98
00:03:35,380 --> 00:03:37,350
Like what my character said...

99
00:03:37,390 --> 00:03:39,510
Someone as clueless as him

100
00:03:39,530 --> 00:03:41,100
could never make a move on their own.

101
00:03:41,120 --> 00:03:42,610
He'll never realize that

102
00:03:42,630 --> 00:03:43,810
he has a crush on Jane.

103
00:03:43,830 --> 00:03:46,190
So Khanoon is the character

104
00:03:46,210 --> 00:03:48,920
who pushes things along

105
00:03:48,940 --> 00:03:51,200
so that Jaab finally realizes it.

106
00:03:51,220 --> 00:03:53,730
I've got eyes.
I can see it, but he can't.

107
00:03:53,750 --> 00:03:55,620
So I'll use these eyes to show him

108
00:03:55,630 --> 00:03:56,360
that, well...

109
00:03:56,370 --> 00:03:58,160
there's something going on between them,

110
00:03:58,200 --> 00:03:59,870
and it's time he made a move.

111
00:03:59,890 --> 00:04:02,250
And if he doesn't know how to flirt,
he can ask me.

112
00:04:02,270 --> 00:04:04,700
Chomphoo is an assistant director

113
00:04:04,720 --> 00:04:06,700
on a film set...

114
00:04:06,790 --> 00:04:08,620
She's bold,

115
00:04:08,640 --> 00:04:10,650
organized,

116
00:04:10,670 --> 00:04:12,120
articulate, and...

117
00:04:12,150 --> 00:04:14,230
has a bit of a boyish edge to her.

118
00:04:14,250 --> 00:04:17,230
[What charm do these characters have
that will win the audience over?]

119
00:04:17,410 --> 00:04:18,100
Charm?

120
00:04:18,120 --> 00:04:19,510
I'm the top!

121
00:04:20,400 --> 00:04:22,270
Maybe I've got a bit of a cool vibe,

122
00:04:22,290 --> 00:04:25,470
in case queer girls
might be into this character.

123
00:04:25,700 --> 00:04:28,900
I think it's Khanoon's innocence
that makes him so charming.

124
00:04:28,940 --> 00:04:31,750
If you want to have a friend
or someone by your side,

125
00:04:31,770 --> 00:04:33,180
I think you'd want
someone like Khanoon,

126
00:04:33,200 --> 00:04:35,100
who's always there to support you.

127
00:04:35,120 --> 00:04:36,360
He might get annoyed with you sometimes,

128
00:04:36,380 --> 00:04:38,730
but he'll always love you
and never betray you.

129
00:04:38,750 --> 00:04:40,150
And no matter what you want to do,

130
00:04:40,170 --> 00:04:41,970
he'll always have your back.

131
00:04:42,010 --> 00:04:44,140
Pun is a sincere person.

132
00:04:44,160 --> 00:04:46,180
He's straightforward

133
00:04:46,200 --> 00:04:48,100
and honest about his feelings.

134
00:04:48,120 --> 00:04:50,080
He says whatever's on his mind.

135
00:04:50,100 --> 00:04:51,730
When Ai joined the team,

136
00:04:51,750 --> 00:04:53,600
Pun fell for him at first sight

137
00:04:53,610 --> 00:04:55,600
and went all out to pursue him.

138
00:04:55,770 --> 00:04:57,500
I think that's quite an interesting charm.

139
00:04:57,560 --> 00:05:00,670
Ai is a sweet kid at work.

140
00:05:00,700 --> 00:05:04,080
He's lively and a fresh new face
at the production house.

141
00:05:04,100 --> 00:05:07,030
I think a lot of the seniors
will adore him.

142
00:05:07,050 --> 00:05:08,600
Maybe it's his looks.

143
00:05:10,410 --> 00:05:11,180
Just kidding.

144
00:05:11,200 --> 00:05:14,520
Maybe it's because
he doesn't overthink things.

145
00:05:14,550 --> 00:05:16,300
He's easy to understand

146
00:05:16,320 --> 00:05:18,370
and not complicated at all.

147
00:05:18,390 --> 00:05:21,090
He's very easy to approach

148
00:05:21,110 --> 00:05:23,480
because, as I said earlier,
he's pretty wild and impulsive,

149
00:05:23,500 --> 00:05:26,660
and doesn't put on airs around anyone.

150
00:05:26,680 --> 00:05:27,870
I think that's his charm.

151
00:05:27,890 --> 00:05:28,970
Mm...

152
00:05:28,990 --> 00:05:31,100
I think it's

153
00:05:31,120 --> 00:05:32,200
his strictness and meticulousness,

154
00:05:32,220 --> 00:05:34,900
his glances, and...

155
00:05:34,930 --> 00:05:37,080
He doesn't make a scene, but

156
00:05:37,100 --> 00:05:39,020
he stops Jaab when he's about to
do something wrong,

157
00:05:39,030 --> 00:05:40,410
or tease him, and it makes them seem

158
00:05:40,430 --> 00:05:42,290
lovey-dovey, like that.

159
00:05:42,310 --> 00:05:43,600
Which is... really cute.

160
00:05:43,620 --> 00:05:45,990
And his looks, too.

161
00:05:46,020 --> 00:05:47,410
Yeah, because with this series,

162
00:05:47,430 --> 00:05:48,760
we wanted to stay true to the characters.

163
00:05:48,780 --> 00:05:50,010
That's why I dyed my hair

164
00:05:50,030 --> 00:05:53,800
and changed my character
to fit Jane as much as possible.

165
00:05:53,860 --> 00:05:56,840
[Did it take long for you
to understand this character?]

166
00:05:56,860 --> 00:05:58,380
- Very long.
- Why?

167
00:05:58,400 --> 00:06:00,190
I was secretly stressed out because

168
00:06:00,220 --> 00:06:03,180
he's extremely different from me.

169
00:06:03,200 --> 00:06:05,880
For example,
when we first started filming,

170
00:06:05,900 --> 00:06:07,970
I didn't feel like
I understood him all that well.

171
00:06:07,990 --> 00:06:10,390
So many times, I tried
to find ways to become Jaab,

172
00:06:10,420 --> 00:06:11,950
figuring out if this one worked
or the other one did.

173
00:06:11,960 --> 00:06:13,470
So I talked to Art,

174
00:06:13,490 --> 00:06:16,130
who helped me tune in,
until we came to the conclusion that

175
00:06:16,150 --> 00:06:17,990
Jaab doesn't overthink anything.

176
00:06:18,010 --> 00:06:19,630
So I chose not to think

177
00:06:19,650 --> 00:06:22,460
when I played him,
and it ended up working

178
00:06:22,480 --> 00:06:25,490
because Jaab...
always has positive energy,

179
00:06:25,510 --> 00:06:27,860
and he doesn't think much
of anyone or anything,

180
00:06:27,880 --> 00:06:29,120
which is not who I am.

181
00:06:29,140 --> 00:06:31,160
But after tuning into him,
I could feel that

182
00:06:31,180 --> 00:06:32,650
I understood him more.

183
00:06:32,670 --> 00:06:36,020
And it felt really good since Jaab
introduced me to new perspectives

184
00:06:36,040 --> 00:06:37,550
and a new attitude toward life.

185
00:06:37,570 --> 00:06:41,460
I think things don't
actually have to be that complicated.

186
00:06:41,500 --> 00:06:42,990
Just be positive, always.

187
00:06:43,010 --> 00:06:45,890
First of all, Jane works in production.

188
00:06:45,910 --> 00:06:49,220
I can relate to him...
I studied film back when I was in school,

189
00:06:49,250 --> 00:06:51,010
so I can put what I learned to use.

190
00:06:51,030 --> 00:06:53,150
The vibe at work,

191
00:06:53,180 --> 00:06:55,440
the people I have to meet, or, like...

192
00:06:55,470 --> 00:06:57,920
everything I've learned came in handy

193
00:06:57,940 --> 00:06:58,940
when playing this character.

194
00:06:58,960 --> 00:07:01,520
But there are certain traits of Jane

195
00:07:01,540 --> 00:07:03,730
that are different from mine.

196
00:07:03,750 --> 00:07:07,140
So that came into play
as I dropped my energy,

197
00:07:07,160 --> 00:07:08,800
but not to the point
that he's blue or quiet.

198
00:07:08,820 --> 00:07:10,700
I'm usually a very active person.

199
00:07:10,720 --> 00:07:12,140
I'm funny and all that.

200
00:07:12,160 --> 00:07:14,570
I just had to tone those down

201
00:07:14,590 --> 00:07:16,100
to take work more seriously

202
00:07:16,120 --> 00:07:18,110
so that I looked more mature.

203
00:07:18,150 --> 00:07:21,540
For Pun, I had quite a bit of time
to go through workshops for the character.

204
00:07:21,560 --> 00:07:22,870
But in the meantime...

205
00:07:22,870 --> 00:07:25,800
I also constantly
tried to understand who he is.

206
00:07:25,800 --> 00:07:27,930
It's my first time acting in a series, and...

207
00:07:27,950 --> 00:07:29,270
I've never been an intern,

208
00:07:29,290 --> 00:07:31,520
so I did a bit of prep work

209
00:07:31,540 --> 00:07:33,540
to understand

210
00:07:33,560 --> 00:07:36,390
how this character would carry himself
as the new kid in a company,

211
00:07:36,400 --> 00:07:38,860
how he would approach the seniors

212
00:07:38,880 --> 00:07:40,780
if he wanted to become close with them, or...

213
00:07:40,800 --> 00:07:43,630
if there were any specific ways
I could carry myself

214
00:07:43,650 --> 00:07:45,900
as a lovely new kid whom people adored.

215
00:07:45,920 --> 00:07:47,330
Prep work is a must for every role.

216
00:07:47,350 --> 00:07:49,460
Even though each character
is close to who I am,

217
00:07:49,480 --> 00:07:51,790
I've gotta say that the voice register I use

218
00:07:51,790 --> 00:07:53,070
is different for each one,

219
00:07:53,080 --> 00:07:56,060
and so is how the energy builds.

220
00:07:56,080 --> 00:07:58,990
On set, I toned it down
compared to the last series I played.

221
00:07:59,010 --> 00:08:00,440
That's the kind of homework I did.

222
00:08:00,470 --> 00:08:03,290
Another bit of homework I did
was to make everyone feel the chemistry

223
00:08:03,310 --> 00:08:05,720
between friends, so that you could tell

224
00:08:05,740 --> 00:08:08,270
Khanoon and Jaab
had been close since childhood,

225
00:08:08,270 --> 00:08:09,190
something like that.

226
00:08:09,190 --> 00:08:13,240
I spent quite a bit of time trying to understand
the character, but not too long because

227
00:08:13,260 --> 00:08:16,180
she's similar to me in some ways,

228
00:08:16,190 --> 00:08:19,600
so it wasn't that hard
for me to get Chomphoo.

229
00:08:19,620 --> 00:08:23,020
It's because after work,
I became familiar with the vibe on set,

230
00:08:23,040 --> 00:08:25,070
and I looked up to many people on set

231
00:08:25,090 --> 00:08:29,470
as examples of what an AD is like.

232
00:08:29,490 --> 00:08:32,470
[Is there any side
of the character that resembles you?]

233
00:08:32,490 --> 00:08:34,340
It probably has more to do with work

234
00:08:34,350 --> 00:08:36,640
because I, Tonliew, am serious about work.

235
00:08:36,660 --> 00:08:37,840
I want a good outcome from my work.

236
00:08:37,840 --> 00:08:39,510
The same goes for Jane. He's serious,

237
00:08:39,510 --> 00:08:41,600
so we kinda have that in common.

238
00:08:41,620 --> 00:08:45,670
But I feel like we're different in some ways,

239
00:08:45,690 --> 00:08:47,520
probably when it comes to how I become stern

240
00:08:47,540 --> 00:08:49,860
when something's not okay.

241
00:08:49,880 --> 00:08:51,280
That's different.

242
00:08:51,300 --> 00:08:53,500
Also, Jane is very reserved.

243
00:08:53,520 --> 00:08:54,310
He's like neatly folded clothes,

244
00:08:54,340 --> 00:08:56,980
but I'm like a pile of clothes

245
00:08:57,010 --> 00:08:58,600
you pile up after doing the laundry.

246
00:08:59,780 --> 00:09:01,760
So we're very different, yeah...

247
00:09:01,780 --> 00:09:04,650
We're both juniors in the company.

248
00:09:04,670 --> 00:09:06,900
In real life, I'm also Bever's junior,

249
00:09:06,920 --> 00:09:08,420
just like Pun and Jaab,

250
00:09:08,440 --> 00:09:10,820
with that senior-junior relationship
in a company and all that.

251
00:09:10,840 --> 00:09:13,800
Probably the energy around friends,

252
00:09:13,870 --> 00:09:15,590
but those from high school, though,

253
00:09:15,610 --> 00:09:18,460
because that's how I talked back in school.

254
00:09:18,480 --> 00:09:20,350
I mean, I was pretty rough-edged,

255
00:09:20,370 --> 00:09:22,610
pretty impolite, and pretty random

256
00:09:22,640 --> 00:09:23,740
around my high school friends.

257
00:09:23,760 --> 00:09:27,100
So, the way I tuned in
to the character was by

258
00:09:27,120 --> 00:09:29,580
catching up with them,

259
00:09:29,610 --> 00:09:31,400
letting it sink in that

260
00:09:31,420 --> 00:09:33,720
I could apply those traits to the series,

261
00:09:33,750 --> 00:09:34,450
because...

262
00:09:34,470 --> 00:09:37,750
the side of me I show to my high school friends
is different from the side

263
00:09:37,750 --> 00:09:38,710
I show to my friends at work.

264
00:09:38,710 --> 00:09:39,810
They're not the same.

265
00:09:39,830 --> 00:09:41,180
With friends, I can...

266
00:09:41,210 --> 00:09:43,720
talk however I want
and be as crazy as I want. It's...

267
00:09:43,740 --> 00:09:45,000
the vibe you share with friends.

268
00:09:45,030 --> 00:09:47,590
But when I step into the new, real world,

269
00:09:47,610 --> 00:09:49,030
I have to adapt a lot.

270
00:09:49,050 --> 00:09:51,990
I have to think more before I talk and all that.

271
00:09:52,160 --> 00:09:52,700
We're both playful.

272
00:09:52,720 --> 00:09:54,310
Jaab and Khanoon are random.

273
00:09:54,330 --> 00:09:56,790
If they sat together for a meal,
they'd never finish eating.

274
00:09:56,810 --> 00:09:57,810
But with Jane...

275
00:09:57,840 --> 00:09:59,700
"Hey, Jaab, you're being ridiculous."

276
00:09:59,720 --> 00:10:00,720
Eat your food.

277
00:10:00,740 --> 00:10:01,390
Jaab would listen.

278
00:10:01,390 --> 00:10:02,990
Since Jaab wouldn't talk to Khanoon anymore,

279
00:10:03,010 --> 00:10:04,240
he'd just be quiet and keep eating.

280
00:10:04,260 --> 00:10:06,290
That's how they finish their food.
They wouldn't, otherwise.

281
00:10:06,310 --> 00:10:08,580
Chomphoo is... a bit articulate.

282
00:10:08,610 --> 00:10:10,790
She's tough, not extremely feminine

283
00:10:10,820 --> 00:10:11,670
or a girly girl.

284
00:10:11,700 --> 00:10:14,430
She's a little bossy like I am.

285
00:10:14,590 --> 00:10:16,370
Well, I think the similarity between us

286
00:10:16,400 --> 00:10:17,680
is that Ai has just started his internship,

287
00:10:17,720 --> 00:10:20,310
and I've also just joined the company,

288
00:10:20,340 --> 00:10:22,190
like, just signed the contract.

289
00:10:22,460 --> 00:10:24,120
So I think we're similar,

290
00:10:24,140 --> 00:10:26,390
since I'm still
getting to know people in the company,

291
00:10:26,410 --> 00:10:30,210
just like Ai is getting to know
the seniors at work.

292
00:10:30,600 --> 00:10:32,120
[If you can choose one word to describe

293
00:10:32,130 --> 00:10:33,600
Jaab and Jane's
relationship, what would it be?]

294
00:10:33,620 --> 00:10:35,910
"Aha." There you go. "Aha."

295
00:10:36,300 --> 00:10:38,100
They're cute together and all that.

296
00:10:38,140 --> 00:10:39,780
I was secretly squealing behind...

297
00:10:40,190 --> 00:10:42,040
behind the monitor.

298
00:10:42,130 --> 00:10:44,650
I think it's... "Cutie patootie."

299
00:10:44,670 --> 00:10:46,030
Cutie patootie is for Jane.

300
00:10:46,050 --> 00:10:46,930
That's for Tonliew.

301
00:10:46,960 --> 00:10:50,290
Meeting Tonliew, I thought, "He's so small."

302
00:10:50,320 --> 00:10:53,480
And when he speaks, his voice is monotonous,

303
00:10:53,500 --> 00:10:55,690
so that's something specific to him.

304
00:10:55,710 --> 00:10:56,820
No matter where he is,

305
00:10:56,850 --> 00:10:57,890
no matter what relationship

306
00:10:57,910 --> 00:11:00,320
or situation he's in, he's a "cutie patootie."

307
00:11:00,350 --> 00:11:01,660
If Tonliew is a cutie patootie,

308
00:11:01,680 --> 00:11:03,660
then I'd say Bever is a "patootie cutie."

309
00:11:03,680 --> 00:11:04,230
Thank you.

310
00:11:04,260 --> 00:11:07,000
I'll go with... "Confusion."

311
00:11:07,040 --> 00:11:08,470
They're both kinda confused.

312
00:11:08,550 --> 00:11:09,900
Jaab doesn't know...

313
00:11:09,930 --> 00:11:11,110
that he likes Jane,

314
00:11:11,130 --> 00:11:12,430
so he's confused, like,

315
00:11:12,460 --> 00:11:13,970
"Wait, am I into Jane?"

316
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:15,480
And with Jane, Jaab's kinda like,

317
00:11:15,500 --> 00:11:18,630
"After all this I've done every day,
you still don't know I'm into you?"

318
00:11:18,630 --> 00:11:19,110
Something like that.

319
00:11:19,110 --> 00:11:20,960
Since he hasn't been in that situation,

320
00:11:20,990 --> 00:11:21,700
he's confused by
the change in Jaab,

321
00:11:21,710 --> 00:11:23,970
wondering how
Jaab feels about him.

322
00:11:23,990 --> 00:11:27,100
With those combined,
there's a certain confusion going on.

323
00:11:27,180 --> 00:11:28,390
That's obvious.

324
00:11:28,410 --> 00:11:30,770
One word that describes
Jaab and Jane's relationship is

325
00:11:30,790 --> 00:11:31,790
"besties."

326
00:11:31,820 --> 00:11:32,930
I think that, in life...

327
00:11:32,930 --> 00:11:36,550
as someone from the countryside
coming to work in Bangkok,

328
00:11:36,700 --> 00:11:39,720
Jaab is the first person
I've felt really close to,

329
00:11:39,740 --> 00:11:43,610
and he makes it easier for me to live in Bangkok

330
00:11:43,630 --> 00:11:47,040
without being afraid to do anything at all.

331
00:11:47,060 --> 00:11:48,260
It feels safe.

332
00:11:48,280 --> 00:11:49,620
One word or sentence

333
00:11:49,630 --> 00:11:50,740
- for JaabJane...
- Yes.

334
00:11:50,790 --> 00:11:52,110
I'll go with

335
00:11:52,130 --> 00:11:53,410
"one-sided."

336
00:11:53,430 --> 00:11:54,980
As to what that's about,

337
00:11:54,990 --> 00:11:56,860
find out in the series.

338
00:11:56,880 --> 00:11:59,540
For Jaab and Jane...

339
00:11:59,560 --> 00:12:00,880
Jane's a "caterpillar,"

340
00:12:01,460 --> 00:12:02,880
the kind on green leaves,

341
00:12:02,910 --> 00:12:05,710
since he's a pest.

342
00:12:05,730 --> 00:12:08,190
Like Jaab says, he's a pest.

343
00:12:08,220 --> 00:12:10,710
And Jaab is a "butterfly,"

344
00:12:10,730 --> 00:12:12,440
one that's already matured

345
00:12:12,460 --> 00:12:13,340
and experienced the world.

346
00:12:13,360 --> 00:12:15,590
And... Jane's still clueless,

347
00:12:15,610 --> 00:12:17,700
and Jaab helps

348
00:12:17,810 --> 00:12:19,750
the caterpillar turn into a butterfly!

349
00:12:19,770 --> 00:12:22,780
[What do you think about love
on set or in the workplace?]

350
00:12:22,800 --> 00:12:24,730
I think it's nothing special.

351
00:12:24,800 --> 00:12:26,310
You can find love anywhere, right?

352
00:12:27,990 --> 00:12:31,310
Once we get closer and
spend more time together,

353
00:12:31,330 --> 00:12:34,690
we start seeing each other's adorable sides.

354
00:12:34,710 --> 00:12:36,790
But sometimes, you have to consider...

355
00:12:36,820 --> 00:12:38,280
whether that love is right or wrong.

356
00:12:38,310 --> 00:12:41,170
If it's wrong,
you have to hold yourself back.

357
00:12:41,170 --> 00:12:42,190
Like Jaab, for example.

358
00:12:42,190 --> 00:12:44,320
When he realizes Jane has feelings for Mon,
he has to hold himself back.

359
00:12:44,320 --> 00:12:45,430
"Hey, no.

360
00:12:45,430 --> 00:12:47,280
He's already with someone...

361
00:12:47,300 --> 00:12:48,590
I need to step back.

362
00:12:48,610 --> 00:12:51,530
But if it's right, then it's kinda sweet.

363
00:12:51,550 --> 00:12:52,920
It's cute and lovely.

364
00:12:52,940 --> 00:12:55,630
It makes you excited to go to work,

365
00:12:55,650 --> 00:12:57,900
like, "Hey, I'll get to see this person

366
00:12:58,250 --> 00:12:59,410
every day."

367
00:12:59,430 --> 00:13:00,910
I think it's lovely.

368
00:13:01,060 --> 00:13:02,670
For me, I think...

369
00:13:02,690 --> 00:13:06,340
love and work can be kept separate.

370
00:13:06,360 --> 00:13:07,600
Work is a responsibility.

371
00:13:07,620 --> 00:13:08,710
Love is a feeling.

372
00:13:08,730 --> 00:13:10,210
So, naturally, they're separate.

373
00:13:10,230 --> 00:13:11,230
We have feelings,

374
00:13:11,250 --> 00:13:12,510
but we also have our jobs to do.

375
00:13:12,530 --> 00:13:14,460
We need to take care of our work first

376
00:13:14,480 --> 00:13:16,020
before dealing with our feelings.

377
00:13:16,050 --> 00:13:18,140
I think Jane is probably the same.

378
00:13:18,160 --> 00:13:20,330
He's probably a reasonable person.

379
00:13:20,350 --> 00:13:22,770
Whether it's work or his feelings,

380
00:13:22,770 --> 00:13:24,060
he can probably keep them separate too.

381
00:13:24,060 --> 00:13:25,710
I think it can work.

382
00:13:25,730 --> 00:13:27,880
Is it a forbidden love, though?

383
00:13:27,900 --> 00:13:29,340
I guess it depends on

384
00:13:29,360 --> 00:13:30,980
what the two people are like,

385
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:32,810
and how well they can

386
00:13:32,840 --> 00:13:34,350
separate love from work.

387
00:13:34,370 --> 00:13:35,590
I believe it's possible.

388
00:13:35,620 --> 00:13:37,850
I think... it's possible.

389
00:13:37,870 --> 00:13:41,180
Love and bonds can develop anywhere.

390
00:13:41,200 --> 00:13:42,970
Yeah, through working together...

391
00:13:42,970 --> 00:13:45,810
or just having the right chemistry
and clicking.

392
00:13:45,810 --> 00:13:47,810
Like I said, I think it's possible.

393
00:13:47,830 --> 00:13:49,480
It's not like I've never seen it happen.

394
00:13:49,500 --> 00:13:51,290
When I'm working on a film set...

395
00:13:51,310 --> 00:13:52,650
I know everyone's exhausted,

396
00:13:52,670 --> 00:13:53,870
but there are always some people

397
00:13:53,890 --> 00:13:56,830
who tease each other back and forth.

398
00:13:56,850 --> 00:13:58,250
So I'll tease them, like,
"Hey, are you two flirting?"

399
00:13:58,250 --> 00:13:59,050
Something like that.

400
00:13:59,050 --> 00:14:02,120
Like, the lighting team might flirt
with someone from the catering team.

401
00:14:02,140 --> 00:14:03,380
Things like that.

402
00:14:03,400 --> 00:14:04,720
Working on a film set...

403
00:14:04,720 --> 00:14:07,000
we have to spend so much time together,

404
00:14:07,030 --> 00:14:08,290
almost 24 hours a day.

405
00:14:08,290 --> 00:14:11,030
We work from 6 A.M. until 10 P.M.

406
00:14:11,050 --> 00:14:13,080
We have to support
and encourage each other.

407
00:14:13,100 --> 00:14:14,130
That's why I think

408
00:14:14,130 --> 00:14:16,420
love on a film set
isn't as far-fetched as it seems.

409
00:14:16,420 --> 00:14:17,540
It's definitely possible.

410
00:14:17,560 --> 00:14:19,120
This kind of love

411
00:14:19,150 --> 00:14:22,190
can feel like forbidden love
when you're working on a film set.

412
00:14:22,210 --> 00:14:24,300
Say you have feelings for each other,

413
00:14:24,320 --> 00:14:26,950
or something happens that hurts one of you,

414
00:14:26,950 --> 00:14:28,790
it can make working together difficult.

415
00:14:28,790 --> 00:14:30,420
We have to work as a team.

416
00:14:30,440 --> 00:14:32,220
Well, it could happen.

417
00:14:32,240 --> 00:14:35,520
You'll have to watch
the series to find out.

418
00:14:35,520 --> 00:14:36,730
Yeah...

419
00:14:36,730 --> 00:14:38,090
- Where are you going?
- I'm waiting for the day

420
00:14:38,110 --> 00:14:41,080
Jane calls Jaab an asshole.

421
00:14:41,100 --> 00:14:42,470
The beers are on me.

422
00:14:42,490 --> 00:14:43,200
Jaab.

423
00:14:44,400 --> 00:14:46,540
I think with someone like Jaab,

424
00:14:46,610 --> 00:14:47,810
it won't be long.

425
00:14:47,830 --> 00:14:48,930
You're the most senior one here.

426
00:14:48,960 --> 00:14:50,580
- Most senior, huh?
- Hey.

427
00:14:50,600 --> 00:14:51,320
Ow.

428
00:14:51,600 --> 00:14:53,940
You two are all lovey-dovey again.

429
00:14:54,020 --> 00:14:54,850
Whoa!

430
00:14:56,890 --> 00:14:58,820
Do you think the male lead
looks a bit weird?

431
00:15:01,250 --> 00:15:02,400
What are you looking at, Jaab?

432
00:15:02,990 --> 00:15:04,230
You're a pest.

433
00:15:06,330 --> 00:15:07,190
What?

434
00:15:07,570 --> 00:15:08,320
Huh?

435
00:15:08,900 --> 00:15:10,420
You had grapes yesterday,

436
00:15:10,460 --> 00:15:11,870
- and you've got oranges today.
- Jane!

437
00:15:11,890 --> 00:15:14,380
Jane... you're like a pest.

438
00:15:15,200 --> 00:15:16,570
Are you saying I'm a worm, Jaab?

439
00:15:17,170 --> 00:15:19,110
I wouldn't have known what to do

440
00:15:19,130 --> 00:15:21,150
if not for you, Pun.

441
00:15:21,700 --> 00:15:22,870
Jane, do you know...

442
00:15:23,620 --> 00:15:24,930
I've never loved anyone before?

443
00:15:24,950 --> 00:15:27,940
[Were there any scenes in the script
that you thought would be fun to play?]

444
00:15:27,970 --> 00:15:29,390
For me?

445
00:15:29,410 --> 00:15:31,680
It's the scene where Jaab

446
00:15:31,700 --> 00:15:33,040
goes to Jane's garden house,

447
00:15:33,060 --> 00:15:35,500
and talks to his friend,

448
00:15:35,520 --> 00:15:38,570
asking for advice about love and work.

449
00:15:38,590 --> 00:15:40,360
They're secretly talking,

450
00:15:40,390 --> 00:15:43,000
when Jane comes in to spray
them with mosquito repellent.

451
00:15:43,020 --> 00:15:44,510
- Oh.
- And because

452
00:15:44,530 --> 00:15:45,910
they're alone together,

453
00:15:45,910 --> 00:15:46,950
the mood is just right.

454
00:15:46,950 --> 00:15:49,960
They get to tease and play around.

455
00:15:49,990 --> 00:15:51,580
Then Aunt comes out to
call them for a meal.

456
00:15:51,610 --> 00:15:53,390
And he looks stunned.

457
00:15:53,410 --> 00:15:55,050
Then... he walks away.

458
00:15:55,070 --> 00:15:56,020
Then he says,

459
00:15:56,050 --> 00:15:57,050
"Stir-fried chayote."

460
00:15:57,070 --> 00:15:58,470
- Chayote...
- Chayote.

461
00:15:58,790 --> 00:16:01,290
- Stir-fried chayote.
- It's funny, like, "what the heck?"

462
00:16:01,310 --> 00:16:02,490
Mine's the same,

463
00:16:02,510 --> 00:16:05,220
but it's the scene where Jaab

464
00:16:05,240 --> 00:16:07,510
talks to his friend Mek first.

465
00:16:07,530 --> 00:16:09,490
He imagines, like, "Hey,

466
00:16:09,510 --> 00:16:12,900
when we go to Jane's place,
we'll have a romantic scene together."

467
00:16:12,920 --> 00:16:14,980
We'll dress like we're in Korea,

468
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:17,080
wearing fur coats and stuff.

469
00:16:17,580 --> 00:16:18,830
He imagines it like...

470
00:16:18,850 --> 00:16:21,530
"Jane... Want a warm hug?"
Something like that.

471
00:16:21,550 --> 00:16:22,880
It's cringey in a way.

472
00:16:23,150 --> 00:16:24,540
And there's the scene where

473
00:16:24,560 --> 00:16:28,010
I have to wear a suit to pick mangoes.

474
00:16:28,030 --> 00:16:30,010
It's such a contrasting scene.

475
00:16:30,030 --> 00:16:32,110
That's why it's my favorite scene.

476
00:16:32,130 --> 00:16:34,540
I like the scenes with Jaab,

477
00:16:34,560 --> 00:16:36,340
or Bever.

478
00:16:36,360 --> 00:16:38,930
I feel like we get to play off each other,

479
00:16:38,950 --> 00:16:40,680
and that's something I'm good at.

480
00:16:40,700 --> 00:16:42,020
I like comedy.

481
00:16:42,040 --> 00:16:45,380
I'm excited to get to act with Bever.

482
00:16:45,400 --> 00:16:46,880
I love improvising,

483
00:16:46,910 --> 00:16:50,100
so I've been looking forward
to playing those scenes.

484
00:16:50,130 --> 00:16:52,560
It's the scene where Chomphoo is working

485
00:16:52,580 --> 00:16:54,780
while the two of them
are being lovey-dovey.

486
00:16:54,800 --> 00:16:56,690
Then Chomphoo comes over
and interrupts them.

487
00:16:56,720 --> 00:16:57,470
It's so sweet.

488
00:16:57,470 --> 00:16:58,870
Then there's the part where...

489
00:16:58,870 --> 00:17:01,380
Jaab gets flustered and stumbles.

490
00:17:01,400 --> 00:17:02,910
It was so cute just reading in the script.

491
00:17:02,930 --> 00:17:04,800
But when we actually filmed it,

492
00:17:04,820 --> 00:17:07,210
it was just as cute. I love that scene.

493
00:17:07,240 --> 00:17:08,730
I think it's the scene where...

494
00:17:08,750 --> 00:17:11,560
Jaab has to go to Jane's place
in another province.

495
00:17:11,620 --> 00:17:12,380
It should be fun.

496
00:17:12,440 --> 00:17:13,960
They'll get to go on a trip.

497
00:17:13,980 --> 00:17:15,390
For me, it's the scene where...

498
00:17:15,410 --> 00:17:17,990
Jaab stops Pun from
saying, "Jaab likes Jane."

499
00:17:18,010 --> 00:17:19,050
He's so innocent.

500
00:17:19,080 --> 00:17:19,670
Very innocent.

501
00:17:19,690 --> 00:17:22,490
There are some really
funny scenes with him and Jaab.

502
00:17:22,510 --> 00:17:24,210
Yeah, I think this one will be fun too.

503
00:17:24,230 --> 00:17:26,230
It's like watching a sitcom, right?

504
00:17:26,280 --> 00:17:27,110
Yeah.

505
00:17:27,130 --> 00:17:29,000
Pun is so innocent,
he doesn't know what to say,

506
00:17:29,000 --> 00:17:30,010
and Jaab goes, "Hey!"

507
00:17:30,010 --> 00:17:31,130
Pun says something, and Jaab goes, "Hey!"

508
00:17:31,150 --> 00:17:32,640
Pun says something,
and Jaab goes, "Hey!" again.

509
00:17:32,660 --> 00:17:34,100
They keep going back and forth.

510
00:17:34,120 --> 00:17:35,020
Yeah.

511
00:17:35,040 --> 00:17:38,030
[What do you think creates
the "chemistry" between Jaab and Jane?]

512
00:17:38,050 --> 00:17:40,150
It comes from a feeling

513
00:17:40,170 --> 00:17:43,180
that develops naturally,

514
00:17:43,200 --> 00:17:45,710
and from how good they feel
when they're together

515
00:17:45,740 --> 00:17:47,590
without having to do much.

516
00:17:47,610 --> 00:17:50,240
I think it's something special because...

517
00:17:50,260 --> 00:17:52,230
chemistry is something that

518
00:17:52,250 --> 00:17:55,090
you never expect to happen.

519
00:17:55,110 --> 00:17:56,530
Jaab himself

520
00:17:56,530 --> 00:17:58,720
works with lots of people, right?

521
00:17:58,720 --> 00:18:01,250
And he's never felt this way
about anyone before.

522
00:18:01,270 --> 00:18:04,510
Then Jane comes along, even though
he's still new, and I think, "Hey,

523
00:18:04,600 --> 00:18:07,420
why does it feel so good
being around this guy?"

524
00:18:07,440 --> 00:18:09,630
Everything about him is so cute.

525
00:18:09,650 --> 00:18:11,120
Yes, because...

526
00:18:11,140 --> 00:18:12,070
It's nice to have you here.

527
00:18:12,100 --> 00:18:13,030
That's right.

528
00:18:13,050 --> 00:18:14,250
You're promoting our partner, huh?

529
00:18:15,680 --> 00:18:17,780
To put it simply,

530
00:18:17,800 --> 00:18:20,560
if Jaab were to fall for someone,

531
00:18:20,580 --> 00:18:22,590
I feel like it wouldn't be Jane,

532
00:18:22,620 --> 00:18:25,020
because he's rough around the edges,

533
00:18:25,050 --> 00:18:27,710
not someone who likes things
neat and proper.

534
00:18:27,730 --> 00:18:28,850
But when he falls for Jane,

535
00:18:28,870 --> 00:18:31,800
all of that goes out the window.
Instead...

536
00:18:31,820 --> 00:18:34,880
whether Jane does something
he likes or dislikes,

537
00:18:34,960 --> 00:18:35,830
he likes it all.

538
00:18:35,850 --> 00:18:37,630
That's why I feel like...

539
00:18:37,660 --> 00:18:40,020
it's a whole new kind of
chemistry for them.

540
00:18:40,040 --> 00:18:42,830
It's like Jaab has discovered
something new in his life that

541
00:18:42,850 --> 00:18:44,160
contrasts with his lifestyle.

542
00:18:44,180 --> 00:18:45,440
And now that it's become part of his life,

543
00:18:45,470 --> 00:18:47,570
it changes his mindset

544
00:18:47,590 --> 00:18:50,160
and outlook on life.

545
00:18:50,180 --> 00:18:52,260
Working on a film set requires teamwork.

546
00:18:52,460 --> 00:18:54,500
Jaab is a director who...

547
00:18:54,520 --> 00:18:56,400
wants the visuals to look beautiful

548
00:18:56,420 --> 00:18:58,650
and everything to turn out
the way he envisions it.

549
00:18:58,670 --> 00:19:00,480
There's no way he could work alone.

550
00:19:00,500 --> 00:19:02,860
He needs someone
who shares a similar vision

551
00:19:02,890 --> 00:19:05,390
and can convey what he sees

552
00:19:05,410 --> 00:19:06,960
through the work itself.

553
00:19:06,980 --> 00:19:09,720
That's where Jane comes in...

554
00:19:09,740 --> 00:19:13,520
He's the bridge that conveys

555
00:19:13,540 --> 00:19:16,470
Jaab's vision to the whole team.

556
00:19:16,500 --> 00:19:17,320
That's the idea.

557
00:19:17,340 --> 00:19:18,480
It's the closeness.

558
00:19:18,500 --> 00:19:20,760
They work together and get to be close.

559
00:19:20,780 --> 00:19:22,270
That's how their chemistry
develops, because

560
00:19:22,290 --> 00:19:25,080
when they get closer,
they get to see sides of each other

561
00:19:25,100 --> 00:19:26,720
that other people don't see.

562
00:19:26,750 --> 00:19:29,950
I think it's their differences
that somehow...

563
00:19:29,970 --> 00:19:31,920
fit together perfectly.

564
00:19:31,940 --> 00:19:35,210
The two halves become whole
when they're together.

565
00:19:35,290 --> 00:19:38,270
The chemistry between Jaab and Jane

566
00:19:38,290 --> 00:19:40,320
comes from their different backgrounds

567
00:19:40,340 --> 00:19:41,830
and struggles.

568
00:19:41,860 --> 00:19:44,180
For Jane, he grew up as

569
00:19:44,200 --> 00:19:45,680
a rich kid from out of town.

570
00:19:45,700 --> 00:19:47,550
Whereas Jaab is more rough and ready.

571
00:19:47,570 --> 00:19:48,560
I think the two...

572
00:19:48,580 --> 00:19:50,950
When they're together, they just make

573
00:19:50,990 --> 00:19:52,920
the perfect contrast.

574
00:19:52,940 --> 00:19:53,670
They're like...

575
00:19:53,670 --> 00:19:56,270
A jock and a nerd.

576
00:19:56,270 --> 00:19:57,370
Something like that.

577
00:19:57,390 --> 00:20:00,370
[What do you think creates
the "chemistry" between Pun and Ai?]

578
00:20:00,390 --> 00:20:02,200
For Pun and Ai...

579
00:20:02,220 --> 00:20:04,240
I'm sure you're wondering...

580
00:20:04,260 --> 00:20:06,770
how Pun is going to
make his move on Ai, right?

581
00:20:06,790 --> 00:20:08,690
You'll have to wait and see,

582
00:20:08,710 --> 00:20:10,710
and cheer Pun on as
he tries to win Ai over.

583
00:20:10,730 --> 00:20:12,680
We'll see how Ai responds

584
00:20:12,700 --> 00:20:16,090
to Pun's feelings.

585
00:20:16,110 --> 00:20:19,110
[Tell us about the charm of
'The Chemistry' that everyone can't miss]

586
00:20:19,130 --> 00:20:20,870
I think the charm of the series...

587
00:20:20,890 --> 00:20:22,740
is seeing what happens when two people

588
00:20:22,760 --> 00:20:25,340
who are polar opposites come together.

589
00:20:25,360 --> 00:20:28,130
One of them is thorough, detail-oriented,

590
00:20:28,150 --> 00:20:29,450
- Mm.
- and methodical,

591
00:20:29,480 --> 00:20:30,650
- Straightforward.
- while the other one...

592
00:20:30,650 --> 00:20:31,480
- goes with the flow completely.
- Chilling.

593
00:20:31,480 --> 00:20:33,350
- He's chill, never overthinks.
- He goes with the flow and is chill.

594
00:20:33,370 --> 00:20:34,200
- Mm.
- Something like that.

595
00:20:34,220 --> 00:20:36,710
When these two
come together and work together,

596
00:20:36,730 --> 00:20:38,380
what would the result be like?

597
00:20:38,400 --> 00:20:39,090
Agreed,

598
00:20:39,120 --> 00:20:42,700
along with the vibe of the whole series.

599
00:20:42,730 --> 00:20:44,890
There are characters like...

600
00:20:44,910 --> 00:20:46,400
Khanoon, Mek,

601
00:20:46,430 --> 00:20:48,160
as well as Bew,

602
00:20:48,180 --> 00:20:49,590
Chomphoo, and all that.

603
00:20:49,610 --> 00:20:52,510
Everyone has such fun energy.

604
00:20:52,530 --> 00:20:54,500
There's also a surprise:

605
00:20:54,520 --> 00:20:57,970
Mon, who comes
into the picture and creates...

606
00:20:57,990 --> 00:20:59,840
- conflicts in their relationship.
- Small conflicts.

607
00:20:59,860 --> 00:21:01,520
Don't think too much of it.
It's fun, easy to digest,

608
00:21:01,540 --> 00:21:02,380
- easy to understand,
- Yes.

609
00:21:02,400 --> 00:21:03,860
- You can jump right to it. It's chill.
- and feel-good.

610
00:21:03,880 --> 00:21:06,970
It's the chemistry between Jaab and Jane,

611
00:21:06,990 --> 00:21:09,220
with jokes,

612
00:21:09,240 --> 00:21:11,100
comedic timing,

613
00:21:11,120 --> 00:21:12,610
drama,

614
00:21:12,610 --> 00:21:15,290
and everything else
for you to cross your fingers for them.

615
00:21:15,290 --> 00:21:18,500
Jaab and Jane get along
like a house on fire too, right?

616
00:21:18,520 --> 00:21:20,810
They live up to
the "Chemistry" in the title.

617
00:21:20,830 --> 00:21:24,100
Please stay tuned and root for these two.

618
00:21:24,120 --> 00:21:25,250
I think you'll like it.

619
00:21:25,270 --> 00:21:26,850
It's also BeverTonliew.

620
00:21:26,870 --> 00:21:28,690
Since the plot is

621
00:21:28,710 --> 00:21:29,880
an office romance,

622
00:21:29,900 --> 00:21:32,280
it might resonate with many

623
00:21:32,310 --> 00:21:34,150
working-age people.

624
00:21:34,180 --> 00:21:35,670
I think it's an interesting storyline.

625
00:21:35,690 --> 00:21:37,990
It hits close to home for all of us,

626
00:21:38,020 --> 00:21:39,470
office romance and all that.

627
00:21:39,550 --> 00:21:40,320
It's relatable.

628
00:21:40,350 --> 00:21:41,320
I think this happens to everyone,

629
00:21:41,320 --> 00:21:42,520
coming home and thinking,

630
00:21:42,520 --> 00:21:43,300
"Are they into me?

631
00:21:43,320 --> 00:21:44,880
Or am I...actually into them?

632
00:21:44,900 --> 00:21:47,120
What's this feeling I'm having?

633
00:21:47,140 --> 00:21:49,160
Darn it, I can't stop smiling.

634
00:21:49,180 --> 00:21:50,060
This is wild."

635
00:21:50,080 --> 00:21:51,320
It's that kinda vibe.

636
00:21:51,320 --> 00:21:52,180
It's something relatable.

637
00:21:52,180 --> 00:21:54,680
The audience will relate
to that feeling when you go,

638
00:21:54,700 --> 00:21:56,640
"Is this the point where I'm into them?

639
00:21:56,660 --> 00:21:57,970
Why am I into them?

640
00:21:57,990 --> 00:21:59,140
How are we gonna flirt?

641
00:21:59,160 --> 00:22:00,890
I still have to work with them.

642
00:22:00,910 --> 00:22:01,840
I have to see them every day.

643
00:22:01,860 --> 00:22:02,720
How are we gonna flirt?"

644
00:22:02,740 --> 00:22:05,210
It's that tangible bliss.

645
00:22:05,230 --> 00:22:06,530
That's the charm of it.

646
00:22:06,640 --> 00:22:08,060
It's in the name.

647
00:22:08,090 --> 00:22:08,900
It's the chemistry.

648
00:22:08,920 --> 00:22:10,560
You have to stay tuned for their chemistry.

649
00:22:10,580 --> 00:22:13,210
No wonder it's Bever and Tonliew.

650
00:22:13,230 --> 00:22:15,550
It's a must-watch. Their chemistry is insane.

651
00:22:15,720 --> 00:22:18,940
It will also show you new sides
of Bever and Tonliew,

652
00:22:18,960 --> 00:22:20,590
and changes in their characters.

653
00:22:20,610 --> 00:22:22,650
I've never seen Bever like this.

654
00:22:22,670 --> 00:22:23,710
Like Jaab, I mean.

655
00:22:23,730 --> 00:22:25,900
On the first day of the fitting,
I was like,

656
00:22:25,920 --> 00:22:27,440
"Ooh, how would Jaab turn out?"

657
00:22:27,460 --> 00:22:30,210
But after several filming sessions,

658
00:22:30,230 --> 00:22:31,500
I looked at him,

659
00:22:31,520 --> 00:22:32,990
and he was so Jaab.

660
00:22:33,010 --> 00:22:34,970
He switched up his character completely,

661
00:22:34,990 --> 00:22:36,450
unkempt and all.

662
00:22:36,470 --> 00:22:38,380
I didn't think Bever could look like that.

663
00:22:38,400 --> 00:22:40,160
Or is that his true self?

664
00:22:40,160 --> 00:22:41,930
[Which part of Jaab and Jane's relationship

665
00:22:41,950 --> 00:22:43,150
feels the closest yet the furthest to them?]

666
00:22:43,680 --> 00:22:44,770
That actually hurt.

667
00:22:44,770 --> 00:22:45,830
Oh, where does it hurt?

668
00:22:46,150 --> 00:22:47,690
- Where?
- Right here.

669
00:22:48,410 --> 00:22:49,590
It's...

670
00:22:49,590 --> 00:22:51,870
a relationship where two people
aren't on the same page.

671
00:22:51,870 --> 00:22:53,760
Jane sees Jaab as a friend,

672
00:22:53,760 --> 00:22:55,370
like a friend-friend.

673
00:22:55,370 --> 00:22:58,210
He thinks Jaab squeezes
his face every day platonically,

674
00:22:58,210 --> 00:22:59,030
which, darn!

675
00:22:59,030 --> 00:23:01,430
No friends squeeze each other's faces like that.

676
00:23:01,430 --> 00:23:02,630
But for Jaab,

677
00:23:02,630 --> 00:23:05,350
that's how he flirts.

678
00:23:05,350 --> 00:23:06,920
Honestly, he doesn't know how to flirt,

679
00:23:06,920 --> 00:23:09,890
so he goes with teasing Jane,

680
00:23:09,890 --> 00:23:11,850
squeezing his face, teasing him,

681
00:23:11,850 --> 00:23:13,000
calling him

682
00:23:13,230 --> 00:23:15,480
"as tiny as a bag," and all that.

683
00:23:15,480 --> 00:23:17,230
That's how he flirts,

684
00:23:17,230 --> 00:23:19,550
which isn't really right, if you ask me.

685
00:23:19,550 --> 00:23:22,290
There's no way for Jane to know
that he's trying to flirt.

686
00:23:22,880 --> 00:23:23,920
After...

687
00:23:23,920 --> 00:23:25,410
spending time together,

688
00:23:25,410 --> 00:23:26,810
Jaab discovers

689
00:23:26,810 --> 00:23:29,270
new sides of Jane that are so adorable.

690
00:23:29,270 --> 00:23:30,520
Poor him, because

691
00:23:30,520 --> 00:23:32,910
knowing that he has...

692
00:23:32,910 --> 00:23:35,150
flowers, fruits...

693
00:23:35,180 --> 00:23:36,680
and Min as friends, you'd go...

694
00:23:36,680 --> 00:23:38,960
"Darn, how does one have this few friends?"

695
00:23:39,610 --> 00:23:42,130
Also, when you find out he was homeschooled

696
00:23:42,130 --> 00:23:44,870
and that he lives in a ginormous house,

697
00:23:44,870 --> 00:23:45,810
you'd feel...

698
00:23:45,810 --> 00:23:47,600
Well, it's not pity per se,

699
00:23:47,600 --> 00:23:49,680
but you'd feel that he'd be lonely,

700
00:23:49,680 --> 00:23:51,960
having gone through all that.

701
00:23:51,960 --> 00:23:53,400
Nothing wrong with that, if you ask me.

702
00:23:53,400 --> 00:23:55,390
It's actually nice because...

703
00:23:55,390 --> 00:23:57,110
it's something I've never experienced,

704
00:23:57,110 --> 00:23:59,590
and I got to see new sides of him.

705
00:23:59,870 --> 00:24:02,280
That pulls Jaab

706
00:24:02,280 --> 00:24:03,910
deeper into the relationship,

707
00:24:03,910 --> 00:24:05,410
and he becomes more into Jane
each time they meet.

708
00:24:05,410 --> 00:24:07,530
That's something I've never experienced.

709
00:24:07,530 --> 00:24:09,290
Getting to know that,
it felt like new territory

710
00:24:09,290 --> 00:24:11,840
in which I wanted to get to know him more.

711
00:24:11,840 --> 00:24:13,190
But at the same time,

712
00:24:13,190 --> 00:24:16,010
he knows Jane doesn't feel that way.

713
00:24:16,210 --> 00:24:17,920
So he has to

714
00:24:17,920 --> 00:24:20,610
contain his feelings,

715
00:24:20,610 --> 00:24:22,250
trying not to get any closer.

716
00:24:22,250 --> 00:24:24,270
Jaab can't put his arm around Jane's shoulders

717
00:24:24,270 --> 00:24:26,320
'cause that's crossing
the line of platonic friendship,

718
00:24:26,320 --> 00:24:28,370
so instead, Jaab has to tickle Jane's waist.

719
00:24:28,370 --> 00:24:30,400
I think it's about trust.

720
00:24:30,400 --> 00:24:32,440
Jane trusts Jaab as his best friend,

721
00:24:32,470 --> 00:24:35,010
the best one in his working life.

722
00:24:35,550 --> 00:24:38,530
But Jaab has fallen too deep, while Jane...

723
00:24:38,530 --> 00:24:41,030
trusts him to be the best friend.

724
00:24:41,030 --> 00:24:41,550
Mm.

725
00:24:41,550 --> 00:24:44,240
So he never thinks
Jaab might have feelings for him.

726
00:24:44,240 --> 00:24:45,890
I guess it's because Jane's cute.

727
00:24:45,890 --> 00:24:46,870
Whoa...

728
00:24:48,150 --> 00:24:49,470
Isn't he cute?

729
00:24:50,720 --> 00:24:53,990
But...when it comes to...
Jane's boundaries with Jaab,

730
00:24:53,990 --> 00:24:58,280
he's very clear about where Jaab stands.

731
00:24:58,280 --> 00:24:59,840
Jane's the one who tells Jaab

732
00:24:59,840 --> 00:25:01,490
when there's someone he's seeing

733
00:25:01,490 --> 00:25:03,130
or when people come into his life.

734
00:25:03,130 --> 00:25:04,820
He's very clear on that part

735
00:25:04,820 --> 00:25:07,610
because Jane can only see him as a friend.

736
00:25:07,610 --> 00:25:10,030
As for Jaab, he integrates himself

737
00:25:10,030 --> 00:25:12,030
- into every moment of Jane's day,
- Exactly.

738
00:25:12,030 --> 00:25:15,210
so when Jaab comes

739
00:25:15,210 --> 00:25:17,080
- into his life,
- It feels good, it does.

740
00:25:17,080 --> 00:25:17,970
it feels good to Jane.

741
00:25:18,670 --> 00:25:20,970
Before Jane knows it,

742
00:25:21,240 --> 00:25:23,320
he can't live without him.

743
00:25:23,320 --> 00:25:24,840
- Mm.
- Mm.

744
00:25:24,840 --> 00:25:27,040
- My heart confesses that I can't be without you.
- Without you.

745
00:25:27,850 --> 00:25:30,850
[How's the vibe on set been
from the first day until now?]

746
00:25:31,320 --> 00:25:32,040
Raining.

747
00:25:32,040 --> 00:25:33,190
Yes, it rains.

748
00:25:33,190 --> 00:25:35,250
We're in the rainy season, and...

749
00:25:35,250 --> 00:25:38,750
we have to really focus on work because...

750
00:25:38,870 --> 00:25:40,130
we have many locations to get through,

751
00:25:40,130 --> 00:25:42,600
and there's also the weather to deal with.

752
00:25:42,600 --> 00:25:43,080
Yes.

753
00:25:43,080 --> 00:25:44,770
So we realized we had to take it seriously.

754
00:25:44,770 --> 00:25:46,840
But in terms of the vibe on set...

755
00:25:46,840 --> 00:25:47,450
it's been so much fun.

756
00:25:47,450 --> 00:25:50,290
We have so many cast members with us this time.

757
00:25:50,290 --> 00:25:51,010
Like I said, there's...

758
00:25:51,010 --> 00:25:52,820
Jara and Jeng.

759
00:25:52,960 --> 00:25:54,920
There's Knomjean,

760
00:25:54,920 --> 00:25:56,050
along with Pentor.

761
00:25:56,050 --> 00:25:59,310
Everyone's already so talkative.

762
00:25:59,310 --> 00:26:02,000
Right after I met Knomjean,
we had to act together.

763
00:26:02,000 --> 00:26:04,610
But she was trying to help me tune in

764
00:26:04,610 --> 00:26:06,170
and break the ice.

765
00:26:06,170 --> 00:26:09,650
Acting with her for the first time,
I was a bit nervous

766
00:26:09,650 --> 00:26:11,410
because I've seen her...

767
00:26:11,410 --> 00:26:12,970
for a very, very long time.

768
00:26:12,970 --> 00:26:14,280
I'm not saying you're old.

769
00:26:14,280 --> 00:26:14,810
I'm sorry...

770
00:26:14,970 --> 00:26:16,850
Playing with her, I was a bit tense,

771
00:26:16,850 --> 00:26:19,560
but she helped ease the tension.

772
00:26:19,800 --> 00:26:21,600
I've already worked with Pentor before,

773
00:26:21,600 --> 00:26:23,130
and I've also met Jeng

774
00:26:23,130 --> 00:26:25,730
during an event for WeTV.

775
00:26:25,730 --> 00:26:27,080
I've also acted with Jara before.

776
00:26:27,080 --> 00:26:31,310
It's that cozy and sweet vibe.

777
00:26:31,310 --> 00:26:34,030
I worked with Ya for the first time.

778
00:26:34,030 --> 00:26:36,320
I was thrilled because I...

779
00:26:36,320 --> 00:26:38,760
- have also seen Ya's work, and...
- Oh, yes.

780
00:26:38,760 --> 00:26:40,880
- That's right.
- Now she plays Auntie Kaew.

781
00:26:40,880 --> 00:26:43,730
It's been so fulfilling
getting to work with seasoned actors.

782
00:26:43,730 --> 00:26:46,560
- It's like I got to learn in the process.
- That's right.

783
00:26:46,560 --> 00:26:48,370
And with the new faces, our boys,

784
00:26:48,370 --> 00:26:49,640
- Prince and Doasao.
- Prince and Doasao,

785
00:26:49,640 --> 00:26:51,530
and such. They're adorable.

786
00:26:51,530 --> 00:26:52,960
They've worked so hard, and...

787
00:26:52,960 --> 00:26:56,630
I feel like younger people make it

788
00:26:56,630 --> 00:26:58,680
lively, and it...

789
00:26:58,680 --> 00:27:01,470
really adds that loveliness to the series.

790
00:27:01,470 --> 00:27:02,550
That's right.

791
00:27:02,550 --> 00:27:03,600
It's been such a blast on set.

792
00:27:03,600 --> 00:27:06,010
When it comes to work, everyone works,

793
00:27:06,010 --> 00:27:08,450
but when it's time to play,
they play to the extreme,

794
00:27:08,450 --> 00:27:10,000
Bever and Tonliew included...

795
00:27:10,000 --> 00:27:11,030
Especially Tonliew.

796
00:27:11,030 --> 00:27:13,830
If he's scheduled to be on set,
he adds color to it.

797
00:27:13,830 --> 00:27:15,190
He's so sweet, and...

798
00:27:15,190 --> 00:27:18,000
I got to see how hardworking they are,

799
00:27:18,000 --> 00:27:20,050
both off-camera and on camera,
so I feel like

800
00:27:20,390 --> 00:27:21,610
the vibe on set has been so pleasant.

801
00:27:21,610 --> 00:27:22,270
As for Doasao,

802
00:27:22,270 --> 00:27:24,770
on my first day on set filming the pilot,

803
00:27:24,770 --> 00:27:26,840
Aloneww walked over to me and said,

804
00:27:26,840 --> 00:27:27,530
"Hey,

805
00:27:27,840 --> 00:27:28,580
Doasao's been quiet.

806
00:27:28,720 --> 00:27:29,920
Can you approach him and chat with him?"

807
00:27:29,920 --> 00:27:32,730
That was my first
responsibility before acting:

808
00:27:32,730 --> 00:27:35,010
doing an ice-breaking session with Doasao,

809
00:27:35,010 --> 00:27:36,450
going, "Hey, what's up? What's your name?"

810
00:27:36,670 --> 00:27:37,370
He was scared.

811
00:27:37,370 --> 00:27:39,690
"I'm just minding my own business.
Why are you talking to me?"

812
00:27:39,690 --> 00:27:40,630
Something like that.

813
00:27:40,630 --> 00:27:42,050
But after we kept talking,

814
00:27:42,050 --> 00:27:43,960
by the last time we met on set,

815
00:27:43,960 --> 00:27:44,670
he was more talkative.

816
00:27:44,670 --> 00:27:45,950
He's expressing himself more.

817
00:27:45,950 --> 00:27:47,130
I asked him to do a TikTok dance,

818
00:27:47,130 --> 00:27:47,930
and he was good at it.

819
00:27:47,930 --> 00:27:49,890
As for the other one,
I didn't know how to do the Brazilian dance.

820
00:27:49,890 --> 00:27:50,890
I asked him, "What's this move?"

821
00:27:50,890 --> 00:27:51,930
There, there.

822
00:27:51,930 --> 00:27:53,120
- Ooh, what do we have?
- Swoosh, swoosh.

823
00:27:53,120 --> 00:27:54,160
How did I learn it?

824
00:27:54,160 --> 00:27:54,840
How?

825
00:27:55,400 --> 00:27:56,010
They both taught me.

826
00:27:56,570 --> 00:27:57,160
Yeah.

827
00:27:57,370 --> 00:27:58,330
They both did.

828
00:27:58,330 --> 00:27:59,810
They helped me learn it, yeah...

829
00:27:59,970 --> 00:28:01,710
So, first of all,

830
00:28:01,710 --> 00:28:03,450
they're both older than me.

831
00:28:03,450 --> 00:28:04,350
I'm not the older one.

832
00:28:04,350 --> 00:28:07,590
And they're both starting to understand

833
00:28:07,590 --> 00:28:09,000
the industry better.

834
00:28:09,000 --> 00:28:11,190
And they're getting ready
to fight alongside the industry.

835
00:28:11,190 --> 00:28:12,270
They can put up a good fight now.

836
00:28:12,270 --> 00:28:13,530
Yeah, they can.

837
00:28:13,530 --> 00:28:14,050
Yeah.

838
00:28:14,160 --> 00:28:16,440
On the first day, it was kinda awkward

839
00:28:16,440 --> 00:28:19,310
because there'd be two more new people on the team,

840
00:28:19,310 --> 00:28:20,770
and we'd never worked with one another.

841
00:28:20,770 --> 00:28:22,040
It was awkward for me at first.

842
00:28:22,040 --> 00:28:24,600
But things got easier as we got to know each other

843
00:28:24,600 --> 00:28:25,880
by working, having fun on set,

844
00:28:25,880 --> 00:28:27,880
chatting, and having snacks together.

845
00:28:28,110 --> 00:28:28,600
He seems like a nice guy.

846
00:28:28,600 --> 00:28:30,350
Bever and TL are generally lovely souls themselves.

847
00:28:30,350 --> 00:28:32,230
They're fun, compatible, and hilarious.

848
00:28:32,230 --> 00:28:33,250
We also took turns napping.

849
00:28:33,850 --> 00:28:35,400
As for Jeng, he's really sweet...

850
00:28:35,400 --> 00:28:37,670
We worked together on another project,

851
00:28:37,670 --> 00:28:39,050
but we really didn't talk back then.

852
00:28:39,050 --> 00:28:40,950
But for this one...

853
00:28:40,950 --> 00:28:44,400
it calls for so much interaction
between their characters.

854
00:28:44,600 --> 00:28:45,350
It's fun.

855
00:28:45,350 --> 00:28:46,880
I got to make more friends.

856
00:28:47,040 --> 00:28:48,190
- How is he?
- Prince is very lovely.

857
00:28:48,190 --> 00:28:50,290
He really is. But at first, he was a bit quiet.

858
00:28:50,290 --> 00:28:52,080
It's like he was too shy to talk.

859
00:28:52,080 --> 00:28:54,230
He was a bit nervous, but as time went on,

860
00:28:54,390 --> 00:28:56,650
the two have their sweet moments, right?

861
00:28:56,650 --> 00:28:59,440
They all sat with their partners,

862
00:28:59,710 --> 00:29:00,680
and had their moments.

863
00:29:01,050 --> 00:29:02,050
It was just...

864
00:29:02,330 --> 00:29:03,080
the two of them.

865
00:29:03,080 --> 00:29:06,310
Bever and TL are lovely and compatible.

866
00:29:06,490 --> 00:29:10,280
When they play their roles,
they look even more adorable.

867
00:29:10,280 --> 00:29:12,790
TL is adorable on his own.

868
00:29:12,790 --> 00:29:16,350
Bever brings a different kind of chemistry.

869
00:29:16,350 --> 00:29:18,590
For Prince and Doasao,

870
00:29:18,620 --> 00:29:21,510
their sweet moments are entirely different.

871
00:29:21,510 --> 00:29:24,310
Although they haven’t talked to others much,

872
00:29:24,310 --> 00:29:26,800
they do their own things a lot

873
00:29:26,800 --> 00:29:28,910
without caring about the world.

874
00:29:29,330 --> 00:29:32,250
[Are there any moments
you still remember fondly?]

875
00:29:32,610 --> 00:29:35,560
It was the emotional scene.

876
00:29:35,560 --> 00:29:37,870
- Yeah, that's what I wanna say, too.
- The emotional scene.

877
00:29:37,870 --> 00:29:40,160
Once Art, the director, called cut,

878
00:29:40,160 --> 00:29:43,070
he complimented us, and he was tearing up.

879
00:29:43,070 --> 00:29:43,840
And I felt like...

880
00:29:43,840 --> 00:29:45,770
I was delighted that

881
00:29:45,770 --> 00:29:47,010
he felt fulfilled with his job.

882
00:29:47,010 --> 00:29:48,830
Yes, I also chose the emotional scene.

883
00:29:48,830 --> 00:29:51,650
It's different from
how he did it when he played Typhoon.

884
00:29:51,650 --> 00:29:53,990
It's a crying scene
that changes the tone entirely.

885
00:29:53,990 --> 00:29:55,560
It's different for Typhoon,

886
00:29:55,800 --> 00:29:57,760
and so is the one for Jane.

887
00:29:57,760 --> 00:30:00,330
I was there, and I could tell that

888
00:30:00,330 --> 00:30:01,990
TL was killing it.

889
00:30:01,990 --> 00:30:04,850
He was able to cry in such a way
that it hit differently

890
00:30:04,850 --> 00:30:06,430
even though they were both crying scenes.

891
00:30:06,430 --> 00:30:08,430
The vibe was totally different.

892
00:30:08,430 --> 00:30:11,480
There was a quote in the trailer.

893
00:30:11,480 --> 00:30:13,470
"It takes a lot to consider someone a friend."

894
00:30:13,470 --> 00:30:15,160
That line gave me goosebumps.

895
00:30:15,160 --> 00:30:16,730
It was incredible.

896
00:30:18,980 --> 00:30:21,330
Everyone on set was really nice to us.

897
00:30:21,330 --> 00:30:22,640
Though we're new,

898
00:30:22,640 --> 00:30:25,410
they helped us and took great care of us.

899
00:30:25,410 --> 00:30:27,910
That's why we didn't feel stressed out
working on this project.

900
00:30:27,910 --> 00:30:28,770
And...

901
00:30:28,770 --> 00:30:31,090
It was a blast.
It felt as if I was actually working in an office.

902
00:30:31,090 --> 00:30:32,280
It was actually my childhood dream,

903
00:30:32,280 --> 00:30:33,450
working at an office.

904
00:30:33,450 --> 00:30:34,550
I love watching office series,

905
00:30:34,550 --> 00:30:36,270
and now I’m appearing in one.

906
00:30:36,270 --> 00:30:38,270
It feels pretty fun, actually.

907
00:30:38,270 --> 00:30:41,790
On set, I was really impressed by

908
00:30:41,790 --> 00:30:43,680
how kind everyone was to us.

909
00:30:43,680 --> 00:30:44,880
Bever, TL, and...

910
00:30:45,520 --> 00:30:47,760
even Doasao did their part really well, as I've said.

911
00:30:47,760 --> 00:30:48,920
Jara and Jeng...

912
00:30:48,920 --> 00:30:51,550
Jara, Jeng, and everyone else
there were very friendly.

913
00:30:51,550 --> 00:30:52,510
TL snores in his sleep.

914
00:30:52,510 --> 00:30:53,750
Yeah, but here's the lovely part.

915
00:30:53,750 --> 00:30:54,990
He puts two chairs up against each other.

916
00:30:54,990 --> 00:30:56,280
They were office chairs, and he put them together.

917
00:30:56,280 --> 00:30:58,320
He curled up and slept,

918
00:30:58,320 --> 00:30:59,440
and when he snored, he'd go like...

919
00:31:00,930 --> 00:31:01,830
His shoulders moved.

920
00:31:02,960 --> 00:31:03,360
Like this.

921
00:31:03,360 --> 00:31:04,320
It's... kinda adorable.

922
00:31:04,320 --> 00:31:04,760
Really?

923
00:31:04,760 --> 00:31:06,970
Yeah, I wish I could film that moment...

924
00:31:06,970 --> 00:31:08,030
but he might get upset with me.

925
00:31:08,450 --> 00:31:09,090
He might be like,

926
00:31:09,090 --> 00:31:11,120
"Why did you film me while I was sleeping?"

927
00:31:11,120 --> 00:31:12,310
Not only is he sweet on camera

928
00:31:12,310 --> 00:31:13,870
but he's also sweet off camera.

929
00:31:13,870 --> 00:31:15,370
I'm impressed by the vibe of the crew.

930
00:31:15,370 --> 00:31:18,950
Of course, Art has been professional
since 'Be My Player Two.'

931
00:31:18,950 --> 00:31:21,880
I have no worries about
the atmosphere of the shoot if Art is there.

932
00:31:21,880 --> 00:31:24,880
He can bring out the best...

933
00:31:24,880 --> 00:31:26,730
and the energy of the actors.

934
00:31:26,730 --> 00:31:27,650
When he comes on set...

935
00:31:27,650 --> 00:31:29,630
When he comes over after
directing from behind the monitor,

936
00:31:29,630 --> 00:31:31,600
he can always make the actors smile and laugh.

937
00:31:31,600 --> 00:31:33,220
He's also another person I'm impressed by.

938
00:31:33,220 --> 00:31:34,000
It's Art.

939
00:31:34,330 --> 00:31:35,050
When was it?

940
00:31:35,050 --> 00:31:36,270
I think when it rained.

941
00:31:36,270 --> 00:31:37,410
It was the first day of the flood.

942
00:31:37,850 --> 00:31:39,010
- Really?!
- Yeah!

943
00:31:39,250 --> 00:31:40,880
Nobody could go home

944
00:31:40,880 --> 00:31:41,930
- on that day...
- The traffic was nuts.

945
00:31:41,930 --> 00:31:43,390
The next day, the flood got worse.

946
00:31:43,390 --> 00:31:44,810
I first had this idea.

947
00:31:44,810 --> 00:31:46,320
"Should I stay at a hotel

948
00:31:46,320 --> 00:31:47,200
for a day?"

949
00:31:47,200 --> 00:31:48,800
Fortunately, I changed my mind, or else...

950
00:31:48,800 --> 00:31:49,880
I would've gotten stuck there.

951
00:31:49,880 --> 00:31:52,950
[Was filming production scenes
for the series easy or challenging?]

952
00:31:52,950 --> 00:31:54,840
Since it's a shoot within a shoot,

953
00:31:54,840 --> 00:31:57,210
and they're working in a production house,

954
00:31:57,210 --> 00:32:00,090
dealing with a lot of people on a film shoot,

955
00:32:00,090 --> 00:32:02,800
it feels like we were genuinely on a shoot

956
00:32:02,800 --> 00:32:04,150
that wasn't for the series.

957
00:32:04,150 --> 00:32:05,040
Mm. Yeah.

958
00:32:05,040 --> 00:32:08,120
It was like we were actually working there

959
00:32:08,120 --> 00:32:09,470
as the characters.

960
00:32:09,470 --> 00:32:12,670
This really makes an impact on the characters,

961
00:32:12,670 --> 00:32:14,420
- making us feel more invested.
- Mm.

962
00:32:14,440 --> 00:32:15,560
The vibe was...

963
00:32:15,580 --> 00:32:17,950
It was what we all could see.

964
00:32:17,950 --> 00:32:19,670
I think the only challenge was this.

965
00:32:19,670 --> 00:32:21,430
I’ve never worked as a director.

966
00:32:21,430 --> 00:32:24,210
I have no clue how to act.

967
00:32:24,210 --> 00:32:28,010
For example, I had to ask Art to show me
how to hold a walkie-talkie.

968
00:32:28,010 --> 00:32:29,830
I simply copy everything he does.

969
00:32:29,970 --> 00:32:32,790
The same goes for
the eye contact, movement, and so on...

970
00:32:32,790 --> 00:32:36,120
I don't have the experience,
so I used him as a reference

971
00:32:36,120 --> 00:32:38,070
and put it to use.

972
00:32:38,070 --> 00:32:41,070
When I had to do it for real,
I didn't know how to act.

973
00:32:41,410 --> 00:32:42,950
I’ve never worked as a director,

974
00:32:42,950 --> 00:32:45,650
and I don't know what to do.

975
00:32:45,650 --> 00:32:47,030
It doesn't feel right...

976
00:32:47,030 --> 00:32:48,010
- "It doesn't feel right?"
- Yeah...

977
00:32:48,010 --> 00:32:49,600
I just couldn’t wrap my head around it back then.

978
00:32:49,850 --> 00:32:51,850
But after he showed me, it started to click.

979
00:32:51,850 --> 00:32:52,800
As for the eye movement...

980
00:32:52,800 --> 00:32:54,630
I simply don't have to solely look at the monitor.

981
00:32:54,630 --> 00:32:57,650
I can also look at what’s happening on set
to catch the finer details.

982
00:32:57,780 --> 00:32:58,880
It feels a bit hard.

983
00:32:58,880 --> 00:33:02,360
I don’t know much about production

984
00:33:02,360 --> 00:33:03,850
because I'm new as well.

985
00:33:03,850 --> 00:33:06,690
But after watching them, it feels fun.
It feels real.

986
00:33:06,910 --> 00:33:08,270
It's a shoot within a shoot.

987
00:33:08,270 --> 00:33:09,630
It's pretty fun.

988
00:33:09,630 --> 00:33:12,230
For me, I feel like

989
00:33:12,360 --> 00:33:13,710
it's very challenging.

990
00:33:13,710 --> 00:33:16,170
I'm very new when it comes to this field of work.

991
00:33:16,170 --> 00:33:18,450
So I don't have that much experience.

992
00:33:18,570 --> 00:33:20,880
It’s neither hard nor easy.
It’s more amusing than anything.

993
00:33:20,880 --> 00:33:22,030
This is important because

994
00:33:22,030 --> 00:33:23,270
the way I dress

995
00:33:23,270 --> 00:33:26,350
even looks like what the camera crew wears.

996
00:33:26,350 --> 00:33:29,890
Even Jara dresses up like
the person holding the tablet thingy

997
00:33:29,890 --> 00:33:32,360
wearing the headphones and stuff...

998
00:33:32,360 --> 00:33:34,190
We look identical, so I'm like...

999
00:33:34,190 --> 00:33:35,730
I might've done the research

1000
00:33:35,730 --> 00:33:37,000
on how a cameraman holds a camera

1001
00:33:37,000 --> 00:33:38,290
and the jargon they use.

1002
00:33:38,400 --> 00:33:39,870
But I can also ask them on set later.

1003
00:33:40,010 --> 00:33:41,840
So this isn't as challenging as other projects,

1004
00:33:41,840 --> 00:33:43,450
as I can do my research directly from them.

1005
00:33:43,450 --> 00:33:45,370
For example, I could ask,
"Excuse me, when it comes to lenses,

1006
00:33:45,370 --> 00:33:47,070
which focal length is ideal for this type of shot,

1007
00:33:47,070 --> 00:33:49,440
and is this the pose you do when framing a shot?

1008
00:33:49,440 --> 00:33:50,400
What is it for?

1009
00:33:50,400 --> 00:33:51,310
How do you use the lighting?

1010
00:33:51,310 --> 00:33:54,190
Are there any technical terms
that I can use during an improv?"

1011
00:33:54,430 --> 00:33:56,010
This is one of the projects that...

1012
00:33:56,010 --> 00:33:57,870
is neither the most challenging...

1013
00:33:57,900 --> 00:33:59,510
nor the easiest in terms of research.

1014
00:33:59,510 --> 00:34:00,440
Why is it funny?

1015
00:34:00,440 --> 00:34:01,350
Well, it's the outfit.

1016
00:34:01,350 --> 00:34:02,890
We'd just stand there like their doppelgangers.

1017
00:34:02,890 --> 00:34:04,810
It's like I'm one of the twins.

1018
00:34:04,970 --> 00:34:05,710
Art said,

1019
00:34:05,710 --> 00:34:07,470
"Jeng, you look identical to him."

1020
00:34:07,730 --> 00:34:08,750
And I really did look like him.

1021
00:34:08,750 --> 00:34:10,850
When I dressed up and walked past them...

1022
00:34:10,850 --> 00:34:13,120
More importantly, I'd do my best to act like them.

1023
00:34:13,280 --> 00:34:15,650
Say, this is how I'd sit behind a camera, right?

1024
00:34:16,050 --> 00:34:17,720
But then I copied their poses.

1025
00:34:18,800 --> 00:34:19,440
Like this.

1026
00:34:19,440 --> 00:34:21,360
I look more like a cameraman now.

1027
00:34:21,720 --> 00:34:22,950
I could just copy them.

1028
00:34:23,080 --> 00:34:26,210
I really had to concentrate very hard at first
because it was confusing.

1029
00:34:26,210 --> 00:34:28,230
When they said "rolling," I was like...

1030
00:34:28,230 --> 00:34:30,030
Say, "3, 2, 1, and action," right?

1031
00:34:30,030 --> 00:34:31,160
I had to repeat the order.

1032
00:34:31,160 --> 00:34:33,610
There was a scene where I had to do just that.

1033
00:34:33,610 --> 00:34:37,550
I had to look at the AD on that day...

1034
00:34:37,950 --> 00:34:39,380
I had to copy what Ice did.

1035
00:34:39,530 --> 00:34:41,390
I straight up copied how things were done.

1036
00:34:42,090 --> 00:34:45,120
[A sneak peek at a scene we shouldn't miss]

1037
00:34:45,120 --> 00:34:46,890
I think it's the scene with Mon

1038
00:34:46,890 --> 00:34:49,560
that I don't want you all to miss,

1039
00:34:49,560 --> 00:34:51,600
because it's the highlight of this series.

1040
00:34:51,600 --> 00:34:53,070
For me, the scene you can't miss

1041
00:34:53,070 --> 00:34:56,810
is when Jaab goes looking for
references to shoot a music video at...

1042
00:34:57,000 --> 00:34:58,410
Jane's garden house.

1043
00:34:58,410 --> 00:35:01,600
And I feel like the mood, vibe, and everything

1044
00:35:01,600 --> 00:35:04,850
make these two look so adorable because...

1045
00:35:04,990 --> 00:35:06,190
when they're together, it's like...

1046
00:35:06,190 --> 00:35:07,850
they have this vibe...

1047
00:35:07,850 --> 00:35:11,850
like, can Jaab live by himself or not?

1048
00:35:11,850 --> 00:35:13,670
I think it's just like Bever and Tonliew.

1049
00:35:14,290 --> 00:35:15,370
Yeah, it's like...

1050
00:35:15,370 --> 00:35:17,350
They're so cute together, like...

1051
00:35:17,350 --> 00:35:20,360
Will Jaab be alright?
How will Jane take care of him?

1052
00:35:20,360 --> 00:35:21,530
Will Jane do anything to him?

1053
00:35:21,750 --> 00:35:23,530
Will he tease him or...

1054
00:35:23,530 --> 00:35:24,560
This part is really cute.

1055
00:35:24,560 --> 00:35:26,440
"Why does Jane look like
such an expert?" Stuff like that.

1056
00:35:26,440 --> 00:35:29,030
It's like... it doesn't match his energy.

1057
00:35:29,150 --> 00:35:31,480
It's like a total surprise, you know.

1058
00:35:31,760 --> 00:35:33,680
So, it's the scene where they introduce Mon.

1059
00:35:33,680 --> 00:35:36,790
Everyone is probably waiting
to see who will play Mon in this.

1060
00:35:36,790 --> 00:35:38,390
I must say that Mon is...

1061
00:35:39,450 --> 00:35:40,150
so handsome.

1062
00:35:40,410 --> 00:35:41,170
Want to know who it is, right?

1063
00:35:41,170 --> 00:35:42,390
Want to know, right?

1064
00:35:42,390 --> 00:35:43,320
They're probably waiting.

1065
00:35:43,490 --> 00:35:44,810
Every scene with Jaab and Jane.

1066
00:35:44,810 --> 00:35:45,470
Of course,

1067
00:35:45,470 --> 00:35:47,630
anyone watching 'The Chemistry'
is definitely waiting for Jaab and Jane.

1068
00:35:47,800 --> 00:35:49,550
But if you don't want to miss anything...

1069
00:35:49,550 --> 00:35:50,880
then make sure to catch all my scenes, too.

1070
00:35:52,600 --> 00:35:55,750
The scene I was in with Tonliew.

1071
00:35:55,750 --> 00:35:57,430
And if you want to feel
more excited watching it,

1072
00:35:57,430 --> 00:35:59,270
you should try guessing, like,

1073
00:35:59,270 --> 00:36:00,840
"Hey, was this in the script?" or

1074
00:36:00,840 --> 00:36:02,270
"Did they improvise this?"

1075
00:36:02,270 --> 00:36:04,390
You should look into it,
and it'll be even more fun.

1076
00:36:04,390 --> 00:36:06,290
Because I put many things in there, too.

1077
00:36:06,290 --> 00:36:08,160
I improvised almost every scene because...

1078
00:36:08,160 --> 00:36:11,310
Like what Art said, I'm the one
who brings out the chemistry of...

1079
00:36:11,520 --> 00:36:12,320
friendship.

1080
00:36:12,320 --> 00:36:14,510
So, I don't want to
follow the script completely,

1081
00:36:14,510 --> 00:36:16,640
but I want to make it feel
as real as possible.

1082
00:36:16,640 --> 00:36:18,970
Like, if we were a group of friends,

1083
00:36:18,970 --> 00:36:20,440
how would we talk to each other?

1084
00:36:20,440 --> 00:36:23,870
I also want to... bring in modern trends.

1085
00:36:23,870 --> 00:36:27,930
For example, right now I'm
trying to find an opening to say...

1086
00:36:27,930 --> 00:36:28,960
"Nene, you're awesome."

1087
00:36:30,330 --> 00:36:31,370
I'm just waiting for the right moment.

1088
00:36:31,370 --> 00:36:35,690
I want you to see the scene
where the three of us cross paths.

1089
00:36:36,990 --> 00:36:38,920
The three of us meeting up, and...

1090
00:36:38,920 --> 00:36:40,890
after meeting, they're like...

1091
00:36:40,890 --> 00:36:42,010
a little bit heartbroken.

1092
00:36:42,010 --> 00:36:44,450
I really want you all to watch the scene.

1093
00:36:44,450 --> 00:36:46,030
Let's see who it turns out to be.

1094
00:36:46,030 --> 00:36:47,200
Yeah!

1095
00:36:47,480 --> 00:36:49,030
Let's see who they are.

1096
00:36:49,150 --> 00:36:52,080
[Let's wrap up
by saying something about the series]

1097
00:36:52,080 --> 00:36:57,110
This is something new for Bever and Tonliew.

1098
00:36:57,110 --> 00:37:01,390
It'd be heart-fluttering for sure. Even
Chomphoo was swooning in front of the monitor

1099
00:37:01,390 --> 00:37:03,010
when they were together.

1100
00:37:03,150 --> 00:37:04,880
Anyway, please stay tuned.

1101
00:37:04,880 --> 00:37:06,020
This series is definitely gonna be fun.

1102
00:37:06,020 --> 00:37:07,560
For anyone who's waiting to see

1103
00:37:07,560 --> 00:37:10,030
if I get to say,
"Nene, you're awesome," in the series...

1104
00:37:10,030 --> 00:37:10,990
Just kidding...

1105
00:37:10,990 --> 00:37:14,020
For anyone looking for
a feel-good series to watch,

1106
00:37:14,020 --> 00:37:15,630
since you've been stressed all year,

1107
00:37:15,630 --> 00:37:17,370
this is your time to rest.

1108
00:37:17,370 --> 00:37:20,350
Don't forget to tune in to
'The Chemistry,' everyone.

1109
00:37:20,350 --> 00:37:22,250
It's a series starring Bever and Tonliew,

1110
00:37:22,250 --> 00:37:24,280
and we get to be in it as well.

1111
00:37:24,280 --> 00:37:26,470
I hope everyone supports
this project with lots of love

1112
00:37:26,470 --> 00:37:29,030
and roots for the romance

1113
00:37:29,030 --> 00:37:32,730
between these two along with us.

1114
00:37:32,730 --> 00:37:34,010
This will be awesome.

1115
00:37:34,150 --> 00:37:36,710
And don't forget to cheer for Pun, too,

1116
00:37:36,710 --> 00:37:38,690
to see if he can win Ai's heart.

1117
00:37:38,690 --> 00:37:40,220
I hope Ai will accept his love, too.

1118
00:37:40,220 --> 00:37:41,610
Please support

1119
00:37:41,610 --> 00:37:43,600
'The Chemistry' and...

1120
00:37:43,630 --> 00:37:47,560
the first episode airs on October 29th.

1121
00:37:47,560 --> 00:37:48,750
Yes, every Thursday.

1122
00:37:48,750 --> 00:37:51,030
You can catch it on GMM25

1123
00:37:51,030 --> 00:37:52,530
at 8:30 P.M.

1124
00:37:52,530 --> 00:37:55,480
And you can watch
the uncut version at 9:30 P.M.

1125
00:37:55,480 --> 00:37:58,360
exclusively on the WeTV app.

1126
00:37:58,360 --> 00:37:59,080
That's right.

1127
00:37:59,410 --> 00:38:01,920
The last time I ever came
this close to a chemistry class

1128
00:38:01,930 --> 00:38:03,270
was probably back in high school.

1129
00:38:03,490 --> 00:38:05,400
But the chemistry back then

1130
00:38:05,400 --> 00:38:07,650
and the chemistry
between the two of us right now...

1131
00:38:07,650 --> 00:38:08,750
Alright, Giew...

1132
00:38:08,750 --> 00:38:10,290
are totally different from what I studied.

1133
00:38:10,290 --> 00:38:12,630
So, we're bringing back
the long-take scene...

1134
00:38:12,630 --> 00:38:14,580
Let me check first to see if it works...

1135
00:38:14,580 --> 00:38:15,420
No, we can't!

1136
00:38:15,420 --> 00:38:16,360
Ow...

1137
00:38:17,000 --> 00:38:17,620
Shh...

1138
00:38:17,620 --> 00:38:18,710
What should I do?

1139
00:38:18,710 --> 00:38:20,320
I really want to get along with this guy!

1140
00:38:21,170 --> 00:38:22,470
We're finally here!

1141
00:38:24,440 --> 00:38:25,030
Oh...

1142
00:38:26,190 --> 00:38:28,270
I'm so sorry, Jane.

1143
00:38:28,270 --> 00:38:29,220
It's just that...

1144
00:38:29,350 --> 00:38:30,990
you're below my eye level.

1145
00:38:31,120 --> 00:38:31,830
Jaab...

1146
00:38:31,830 --> 00:38:32,640
- Khanoon.
- Huh?

1147
00:38:32,640 --> 00:38:34,200
- Where are you going?
- I'm waiting

1148
00:38:34,200 --> 00:38:37,030
for the day Jane calls Jaab an asshole.

1149
00:38:37,210 --> 00:38:38,450
The beers are on me.

1150
00:38:38,570 --> 00:38:39,280
Jaab.

1151
00:38:40,380 --> 00:38:42,520
I think with someone like Jaab,

1152
00:38:42,670 --> 00:38:43,820
it won't be long.

1153
00:38:43,820 --> 00:38:44,970
You're the most senior one here.

1154
00:38:44,970 --> 00:38:46,670
- Most senior, huh?
- Hey.

1155
00:38:46,670 --> 00:38:47,250
Ow...

1156
00:38:47,640 --> 00:38:49,750
You two are all lovey-dovey again.

1157
00:38:50,070 --> 00:38:50,690
Whoa!

1158
00:38:51,770 --> 00:38:52,930
[Falling in love Jaab style]

1159
00:38:52,930 --> 00:38:54,450
Do you think the male lead
looks a bit weird?

1160
00:38:57,270 --> 00:38:58,040
What are you looking at, Jaab?

1161
00:38:59,050 --> 00:39:00,220
You're a pest.

1162
00:39:02,360 --> 00:39:03,070
What?

1163
00:39:03,530 --> 00:39:04,320
Huh?

1164
00:39:04,890 --> 00:39:06,480
You had grapes yesterday,

1165
00:39:06,480 --> 00:39:07,850
- and you've got oranges today.
- Jane!

1166
00:39:07,850 --> 00:39:09,990
Jane... you're like a pest.

1167
00:39:11,290 --> 00:39:12,610
Are you saying I'm a caterpillar, Jaab?

1168
00:39:13,730 --> 00:39:14,150
Yeah.

1169
00:39:14,150 --> 00:39:14,730
Hey! Jane!

1170
00:39:14,870 --> 00:39:16,120
- Take this!
- Jane!

1171
00:39:16,120 --> 00:39:17,250
Wanna fight me?

1172
00:39:17,950 --> 00:39:18,820
Do you like Jane?

1173
00:39:20,960 --> 00:39:21,730
I...

1174
00:39:22,040 --> 00:39:22,840
like Jane...

1175
00:39:23,630 --> 00:39:24,480
I think?

1176
00:39:25,910 --> 00:39:26,570
Huh?

1177
00:39:29,030 --> 00:39:29,590
No,

1178
00:39:29,590 --> 00:39:30,640
it's nothing.

1179
00:39:31,670 --> 00:39:33,010
Why did you write on my forehead?

1180
00:39:33,010 --> 00:39:33,870
I'm sorry!

1181
00:39:34,010 --> 00:39:36,780
It was getting in your eyes,
so I tried to brush it away.

1182
00:39:36,910 --> 00:39:38,690
How does that even affect you?

1183
00:39:38,690 --> 00:39:39,390
It does!

1184
00:39:39,390 --> 00:39:40,360
Because I was...

1185
00:39:44,710 --> 00:39:46,480
Do I really like Jane?

1186
00:39:46,930 --> 00:39:47,720
Do I like Jane...

1187
00:39:49,920 --> 00:39:51,850
[Trapped in the Friend Zone]

1188
00:39:52,080 --> 00:39:53,720
I know what's bothering you.
[Goodnight, Jane]

1189
00:39:53,720 --> 00:39:55,220
It's because you found out

1190
00:39:55,470 --> 00:39:56,600
I've been talking to Mon.

1191
00:39:58,670 --> 00:40:00,950
You know how hard it was for me

1192
00:40:01,110 --> 00:40:02,220
to call someone my friend?

1193
00:40:03,430 --> 00:40:05,580
So what are you going to do about Jane?

1194
00:40:05,810 --> 00:40:07,750
Well, whenever you're ready,

1195
00:40:07,750 --> 00:40:08,720
you can tell me about it.

1196
00:40:08,880 --> 00:40:11,980
Because I know a pathetic,
clueless loser like you

1197
00:40:12,120 --> 00:40:13,720
wouldn't know how to flirt anyway.

1198
00:40:13,870 --> 00:40:15,950
Are you worried about me, Mr. Jannarong?

1199
00:40:16,210 --> 00:40:17,980
Yes, I am.

1200
00:40:18,550 --> 00:40:20,420
Who can even take your position?

1201
00:40:22,450 --> 00:40:24,320
[The cliché friends-to-lovers
trope we've all seen]

1202
00:40:24,640 --> 00:40:27,150
Your bag is tiny, just like you, huh?

1203
00:40:27,770 --> 00:40:29,760
This is just like... your pen.

1204
00:40:30,080 --> 00:40:31,210
Totally a brat like you.

1205
00:40:31,610 --> 00:40:32,490
Hey!

1206
00:40:32,790 --> 00:40:33,880
That's cute, though.

1207
00:40:34,750 --> 00:40:37,030
Thanks for picking me up
and dropping me off,

1208
00:40:37,280 --> 00:40:38,920
Mr. Phongkitti.

1209
00:40:39,090 --> 00:40:40,230
- Oh?
- Understood,

1210
00:40:40,600 --> 00:40:41,920
Mr. Jannarong.

1211
00:40:43,030 --> 00:40:44,000
Yay!

1212
00:40:44,120 --> 00:40:46,150
I wouldn't have known what to do

1213
00:40:46,150 --> 00:40:48,120
if not for you, Pun.

1214
00:40:48,690 --> 00:40:50,080
Jane, do you know...

1215
00:40:50,600 --> 00:40:51,950
I've never loved anyone before?

1216
00:40:52,510 --> 00:40:54,570
I've never looked at anyone but you.

1217
00:40:55,380 --> 00:40:59,120
[THE CHEMISTRY]

1218
00:40:59,120 --> 00:41:01,510
[New episodes every Thursday
at 8:30 P.M. on GMM25]

1219
00:41:01,540 --> 00:41:06,720
[Watch the uncut version at 9:30 P.M.
exclusively on WeTV]
